<https://w3id.org/probknow/resource/claim/morphoeval-pringle-roman-esco-fractal-inflorescence> a pk1:Claim ;
    rdfs:label "Azpeitia et al. (2021) TFL1-LFY-AP1/CAL-SOC1 floral GRN perturbation, PIN1 auxin-transport epidermal mesh and accelerating-plastochron Romanesco fractal inflorescence morphogenesis (Brassica oleracea var. botrytis (Romanesco & Cauliflower curds) and Arabidopsis thaliana (ap1 cal mutant))",
        "Azpeitia et al. (2021) TFL1-LFY-AP1/CAL-SOC1 floral GRN perturbation, PIN1 auxin-transport epidermal mesh and accelerating-plastochron Romanesco fractal inflorescence morphogenesis faithfully reproduces Brassica oleracea var. botrytis (Romanesco & Cauliflower curds) and Arabidopsis thaliana (ap1 cal mutant) morphology" ;
    dct:conformsTo <https://w3id.org/probknow/resource/math-law/pringle-roman-esco-fractal-inflorescence-1>,
        <https://w3id.org/probknow/resource/math-law/pringle-roman-esco-fractal-inflorescence-2>,
        <https://w3id.org/probknow/resource/math-law/pringle-roman-esco-fractal-inflorescence-3>,
        <https://w3id.org/probknow/resource/math-law/pringle-roman-esco-fractal-inflorescence-4>,
        <https://w3id.org/probknow/resource/math-law/pringle-roman-esco-fractal-inflorescence-5> ;
    dct:description "The simulation script(s) 2021-pringle-roman-esco-fractal-inflorescence.py implement the cited source model as published and produce forms that match real Brassica oleracea var. botrytis (Romanesco & Cauliflower curds) and Arabidopsis thaliana (ap1 cal mutant) specimens and the source authors' figures. A belief under audit, not a fact: its credibility is the weight of evidence (MorphoEval 0.1.0 overall 71.5/100, audit 2026-10-19-roman-esco-fractal-inflorescence-audit-v3) and the assessments." ;
    dct:subject <https://github.com/fractastical/morpholib/blob/d58a084/2021-pringle-roman-esco-fractal-inflorescence.py> ;
    schema:about "Brassica oleracea var. botrytis (Romanesco & Cauliflower curds) and Arabidopsis thaliana (ap1 cal mutant)" ;
    schema:additionalProperty "does_not_claim: A continuum finite-element solution of PIN1 auxin transport on the curved meristem manifold; cell division or mechanics; the paper's own logical GRN or L-system; angular precision of the emergent phyllotaxis sufficient to generate Fibonacci parastichies (the coupled tree built from the emergent 133.9 deg angle measures (8,16))",
        "reconstructed_in_script: 3D 4-order recursive phyllotactic meristem tree with exact quadratic plastochron initiation times N(T) = r0 T + beta T^2/2, a PRESCRIBED linear envelope H/R(beta) = 0.56 + 10.8235 beta, raw area-weighted 3D box-counting D_f, and MEASURED nearest-neighbour contact parastichies on the generated lattice ((8,13) at beta = 0 and (13,21) for beta >= 0.04 on the curd-scale T = 80 lattice; (3,5) on the per-axis T = 20 lattice)",
        "reconstructed_in_script: Excess-green curd segmentation and two fixed-scale LoG floret detections (86 order-2, 421 order-3 cones) on the SHA-256-locked Romanesco specimen photograph, reported RAW: bounding-box H/R 1.76, lambda 0.390, 2.5D relief box slope 2.36",
        "reconstructed_in_script: RK45 solver for a coupled 4-node continuous Hill ODE GRN (WT g_AP1 = 1, ap1 cal / curd g_AP1 = 0, lfy loss-of-function control) with HAND-TUNED coefficients that hit the vendored steady-state targets (the paper's network is logical, not these ODEs)",
        "reconstructed_in_script: Reduced cell-based PIN1 polar auxin transport (Jönsson 2006 allocation, Smith 2006 sinks/threshold/advection) on a growing jittered k-NN epidermal mesh over cones of H/R 0.56 and 1.48 at three dome radii: emergent initiation rate r_p(R) = -0.16 + 0.36 R (r = 0.99), emergent divergence median 133.9 deg (MAD 25.6), PIN1 polarity index 0.57, T = 0 ablation gives 0 initiations; coupling beta_emergent = (k / r_p(R0)) v_r = 0.289 at the vendored v_r = 0.16 (reference 0.085, implied v_r* = 0.047)",
        "reported_in_source: Azpeitia et al. (2021) Science 373:192-197: loss of AP1/CAL in ap1 cal and Brassica curd meristems abolishes floral commitment while transient LFY induction leaves a SOC1/AGL24/FUL 'floral memory' (bract suppression) and high TFL1 shoot identity, so lateral primordia reiterate spiral phyllotaxis across several branching orders; Cauliflower meristems keep a constant plastochron and form a hemispherical curd, Romanesco meristems grow and initiate ever faster (decreasing plastochron), forming conical self-similar curds with higher Fibonacci parastichy numbers",
        "reported_in_source: Jönsson et al. (2006) and Smith et al. (2006): up-the-gradient PIN1 allocation on a cellular shoot-apex template produces auxin maxima whose threshold-triggered initiation, sink behaviour and outward advection reproduce spiral phyllotaxis near 137.5 deg; Reinhardt et al. (2003): pin1 / NPA apices form no primordia; Douady & Couder (1992): initiation rate scales with the free perimeter of the initiation ring",
        "transfer_boundary: The Kim (2004) D_f ~ 2.71 / 2.38 references were carried from Pass 1 and could not be independently re-verified offline in Pass 3",
        "transfer_boundary: The PIN1 model is a discrete cell mesh with Euclidean (not geodesic) sink fields and a cone approximation of the hemispherical dome; its dimensionless parameters are chosen for the spiral regime, not fitted to Brassica",
        "transfer_boundary: The vendored `plastochron_beta_sweep_benchmark_series`, `genotype_morphometric_benchmarks`, `radial_expansion_rate_v_r` and internode dz values are Pass 1 interpolations/syntheses anchored on the two Azpeitia et al. (2021) end-points, not tables from the paper; agreement with them is self-consistency, not validation" ;
    pk1:aristotelianEfficientCause "4. Polar Auxin & Turgor Stress" ;
    pk1:aristotelianMegistonGenos "III. Phyta (Embryophyta)" ;
    pk1:aristotelianPoionForm "Spirals, Veins & Puzzle Cells" ;
    pk1:aristotelianPosonLaw "Golden Angle / Auxin Flux" ;
    pk1:aristotelianSubalternClass "Angiospermae & Gymnospermae" ;
    pk1:biologicalGenus "Brassica" ;
    pk1:context "script(s): https://github.com/fractastical/morpholib/blob/d58a084/2021-pringle-roman-esco-fractal-inflorescence.py; output: docs/media/roman_esco_fractal_inflorescence_comparison.png; organism: Brassica oleracea var. botrytis (Romanesco & Cauliflower curds) and Arabidopsis thaliana (ap1 cal mutant); checkpoint commit: https://github.com/fractastical/morpholib/commit/d58a084; environment: python 3.14.7, numpy 2.5.4, scipy 1.16.3, matplotlib 3.10.7, Pillow 12.0.0; spec_fingerprint: a6030f05b7cbd188f43ca98602c59735514d8a783a5d591370042c15a25296a0; artifact_sha256: 6a15f43bc46ef0bc731a4c393b12ce1350422559ff7c219fa507b99a16b1892e; input_dataset_sha256: {datasets/roman_esco_fractal_inflorescence/paper_citations.bib=4e4a53dcfd72833a..., datasets/roman_esco_fractal_inflorescence/roman_esco_fractal_inflorescence_reference.json=b580780d055808ce..., datasets/roman_esco_fractal_inflorescence/romanesco_brassica_oleracea_specimen.jpg=5fba6c320b478d6c..., datasets/roman_esco_fractal_inflorescence/scout_manifest.json=d684b2df5ef44398...}; supersedes_audit_id: 2026-10-19-roman-esco-fractal-inflorescence-audit-v2; claim_boundary: [reported_in_source: Azpeitia et al. (2021) Science 373:192-197: loss of AP1/CAL in ap1 cal and Brassica curd meristems abolishes floral commitment while transient LFY induction leaves a SOC1/AGL24/FUL 'floral memory' (bract suppression) and high TFL1 shoot identity, so lateral primordia reiterate spiral phyllotaxis across several branching orders; Cauliflower meristems keep a constant plastochron and form a hemispherical curd, Romanesco meristems grow and initiate ever faster (decreasing plastochron), forming conical self-similar curds with higher Fibonacci parastichy numbers | Jönsson et al. (2006) and Smith et al. (2006): up-the-gradient PIN1 allocation on a cellular shoot-apex template produces auxin maxima whose threshold-triggered initiation, sink behaviour and outward advection reproduce spiral phyllotaxis near 137.5 deg; Reinhardt et al. (2003): pin1 / NPA apices form no primordia; Douady & Couder (1992): initiation rate scales with the free perimeter of the initiation ring; reconstructed_in_script: RK45 solver for a coupled 4-node continuous Hill ODE GRN (WT g_AP1 = 1, ap1 cal / curd g_AP1 = 0, lfy loss-of-function control) with HAND-TUNED coefficients that hit the vendored steady-state targets (the paper's network is logical, not these ODEs) | 3D 4-order recursive phyllotactic meristem tree with exact quadratic plastochron initiation times N(T) = r0 T + beta T^2/2, a PRESCRIBED linear envelope H/R(beta) = 0.56 + 10.8235 beta, raw area-weighted 3D box-counting D_f, and MEASURED nearest-neighbour contact parastichies on the generated lattice ((8,13) at beta = 0 and (13,21) for beta >= 0.04 on the curd-scale T = 80 lattice; (3,5) on the per-axis T = 20 lattice) | Reduced cell-based PIN1 polar auxin transport (Jönsson 2006 allocation, Smith 2006 sinks/threshold/advection) on a growing jittered k-NN epidermal mesh over cones of H/R 0.56 and 1.48 at three dome radii: emergent initiation rate r_p(R) = -0.16 + 0.36 R (r = 0.99), emergent divergence median 133.9 deg (MAD 25.6), PIN1 polarity index 0.57, T = 0 ablation gives 0 initiations; coupling beta_emergent = (k / r_p(R0)) v_r = 0.289 at the vendored v_r = 0.16 (reference 0.085, implied v_r* = 0.047) | Excess-green curd segmentation and two fixed-scale LoG floret detections (86 order-2, 421 order-3 cones) on the SHA-256-locked Romanesco specimen photograph, reported RAW: bounding-box H/R 1.76, lambda 0.390, 2.5D relief box slope 2.36; transfer_boundary: The vendored `plastochron_beta_sweep_benchmark_series`, `genotype_morphometric_benchmarks`, `radial_expansion_rate_v_r` and internode dz values are Pass 1 interpolations/syntheses anchored on the two Azpeitia et al. (2021) end-points, not tables from the paper; agreement with them is self-consistency, not validation | The PIN1 model is a discrete cell mesh with Euclidean (not geodesic) sink fields and a cone approximation of the hemispherical dome; its dimensionless parameters are chosen for the spiral regime, not fitted to Brassica | The Kim (2004) D_f ~ 2.71 / 2.38 references were carried from Pass 1 and could not be independently re-verified offline in Pass 3; does_not_claim: A continuum finite-element solution of PIN1 auxin transport on the curved meristem manifold; cell division or mechanics; the paper's own logical GRN or L-system; angular precision of the emergent phyllotaxis sufficient to generate Fibonacci parastichies (the coupled tree built from the emergent 133.9 deg angle measures (8,16))]" ;
