<https://w3id.org/probknow/resource/assessment/morphoeval-pringle-roman-esco-fractal-inflorescence-code-traceability> a pk1:LLMClaimAssessment ;
    rdfs:label "Azpeitia et al. (2021) TFL1-LFY-AP1/CAL-SOC1 floral GRN perturbation, PIN1 auxin-transport epidermal mesh and accelerating-plastochron Romanesco fractal inflorescence morphogenesis — Code-to-model traceability: 82/100" ;
    dct:date "2026-10-20"^^xsd:date ;
    dct:description "The module docstring maps each law to its equations, its source and its Lean 4 theorem (L1-93); every solver docstring states what it computes, which paper step it follows and — new in Pass 3 — what is prescribed, raw, conditioned or a self-consistency check (L340-356, L482-493, L867-883); the `math_kg_loops` YAML registers Laws 4-5 with lean/code loci. Deductions: the GRN coefficients at L198-223 carry no citation (-6); the tree geometry constants (0.68/0.52 radial exponents, tilt 0.52/0.72, child_scale lambda + 0.14 age_frac, child_t 0.52 + 0.22 age_frac at L429-441) are uncited shape heuristics (-6); the PIN1 parameters are documented as dimensionless choices but the mapping from mesh time to tree time (r0 = 1 per tau) is only in the coupling docstring (-3); Lean `lean_locus` line ranges in the YAML for Laws 1-3 were not re-pinned in Pass 3 (-3)." ;
    dct:subject <https://w3id.org/probknow/resource/concept/morphoeval-0.1.0-code-traceability> ;
    pk1:assessedBy <https://w3id.org/probknow/resource/model/claude-fable-5-1> ;
    pk1:assessmentType "morphoeval/0.1.0/code-traceability" ;
    pk1:evidenceAgainst "2021-pringle-roman-esco-fractal-inflorescence.py L429–L441: Uncited geometric heuristics (radial exponents, tilt, child scale/time factors) <https://github.com/fractastical/morpholib/blob/d58a084/2021-pringle-roman-esco-fractal-inflorescence.py#L429-L441>" ;
    pk1:hasEvidence <https://w3id.org/probknow/resource/evidence/morphoeval-pringle-roman-esco-fractal-inflorescence-code-traceability-1>,
        <https://w3id.org/probknow/resource/evidence/morphoeval-pringle-roman-esco-fractal-inflorescence-code-traceability-2>,
        <https://w3id.org/probknow/resource/evidence/morphoeval-pringle-roman-esco-fractal-inflorescence-code-traceability-3> ;
    pk1:hasScore 8.2e-01 ;
    pk1:hasVerdict "faithful" .

<https://w3id.org/probknow/resource/assessment/morphoeval-pringle-roman-esco-fractal-inflorescence-model-fidelity> a pk1:LLMClaimAssessment ;
    rdfs:label "Azpeitia et al. (2021) TFL1-LFY-AP1/CAL-SOC1 floral GRN perturbation, PIN1 auxin-transport epidermal mesh and accelerating-plastochron Romanesco fractal inflorescence morphogenesis — Model fidelity to source: 72/100" ;
    dct:date "2026-10-20"^^xsd:date ;
    dct:description "Credited: the quadratic plastochron law N(T) = r0 T + beta T^2/2 is exact (L268-286) and the PIN1 mesh implements the Jönsson (2006) allocation P_ij = P_tot A_j / (kappa + sum A_k) with the correct net-transport term, Smith (2006) threshold initiation / sinks / outward advection and central-zone cell production (L637-777); contact parastichies are now a genuine measurement on the generated lattice (L289-337) and the (8,13) -> (13,21) climb emerges from primordium density; five Lean 4 theorems cover Laws 1-5 (0 sorrys). Deductions: the GRN is a continuous Hill ODE with 20+ hand-tuned coefficients (L198-223) that reproduce vendored steady states, whereas Azpeitia et al.'s network is logical (-8); the curd envelope H/R(beta) = 0.56 + 10.8235 beta is prescribed (L388), so Law 3 is an input, not an output of the growth model (-7); the tree is a point skeleton whose children overlap (child_scale 0.38-0.52 with 20-37 children per parent, L415-440) and whose raw box-count D_f is 1.95 vs 2.71, i.e. the model does not produce a fractal surface of the reported dimension (-6); the PIN1 mesh approximates the hemispherical dome by a cone, uses Euclidean sink distances and is not a FEM solve as the v2 item asked (-5); the coupling constant v_r is vendored, not derived (-2)." ;
    dct:subject <https://w3id.org/probknow/resource/concept/morphoeval-0.1.0-model-fidelity> ;
    pk1:assessedBy <https://w3id.org/probknow/resource/model/claude-fable-5-1> ;
    pk1:assessmentType "morphoeval/0.1.0/model-fidelity" ;
    pk1:evidenceAgainst "2021-pringle-roman-esco-fractal-inflorescence.py L198–L223: Hand-tuned Hill coefficients (2.85, 0.18, 1.95, 2.75, 1.15, 1.85, 2.15, 2.52 ...) not traced to the paper, whose GRN is logical <https://github.com/fractastical/morpholib/blob/d58a084/2021-pringle-roman-esco-fractal-inflorescence.py#L198-L223>",
        "2021-pringle-roman-esco-fractal-inflorescence.py L388–L388: H/R(beta) = 0.56 + 10.823529 beta is prescribed; Law 3 is an input <https://github.com/fractastical/morpholib/blob/d58a084/2021-pringle-roman-esco-fractal-inflorescence.py#L388-L388>" ;
    pk1:hasEvidence <https://w3id.org/probknow/resource/evidence/morphoeval-pringle-roman-esco-fractal-inflorescence-model-fidelity-1>,
        <https://w3id.org/probknow/resource/evidence/morphoeval-pringle-roman-esco-fractal-inflorescence-model-fidelity-2>,
        <https://w3id.org/probknow/resource/evidence/morphoeval-pringle-roman-esco-fractal-inflorescence-model-fidelity-3>,
        <https://w3id.org/probknow/resource/evidence/morphoeval-pringle-roman-esco-fractal-inflorescence-model-fidelity-4> ;
    pk1:hasScore 7.2e-01 ;
    pk1:hasVerdict "mostly faithful" .

<https://w3id.org/probknow/resource/assessment/morphoeval-pringle-roman-esco-fractal-inflorescence-morphometric-validation> a pk1:LLMClaimAssessment ;
    rdfs:label "Azpeitia et al. (2021) TFL1-LFY-AP1/CAL-SOC1 floral GRN perturbation, PIN1 auxin-transport epidermal mesh and accelerating-plastochron Romanesco fractal inflorescence morphogenesis — Morphometric validation: 66/100" ;
    dct:date "2026-10-20"^^xsd:date ;
    dct:description "`measurements_from()` (L1277-1399) reports 14 measurements, each with a unit, a reference value, a literature source and a method string that states what was measured and what was not, including negative controls (lfy, beta = 0, T = 0). Credited: the parastichy transition is a real measurement that matches the reference (34 vs 34; 5/6 sweep sums), the ablation ratio is 0.0 vs 0 (Reinhardt 2003), the GRN steady states hit the vendored targets, the perimeter-scaling slope is measured (r = 0.99). Deductions: raw D_f 1.95 vs 2.71 (mean sweep bias -0.79) (-8); beta_emergent 0.289 vs 0.085 is a 3.4x miss, resolved only by an implied v_r* = 0.047 that is not independently supported (-6); emergent divergence 133.9 deg with MAD 25.6 deg and only 32% of events within +/-15 deg of the golden angle is weak quantitative agreement (-5); the perimeter-scaling normalised slope is 1.81 on the cone / 2.06 on the dome against the 1.0 expected for pure perimeter scaling (-3); the H/R Pearson r = 1.0 measurement is a self-consistency check of a prescribed law against an interpolated series and should not count as validation (-4); specimen H/R 1.76 vs 1.48 (-3); lambda = 0.390 is conditioned by the LoG sigma ratio 7/18 = 0.389 (-5)." ;
    dct:subject <https://w3id.org/probknow/resource/concept/morphoeval-0.1.0-morphometric-validation> ;
    pk1:assessedBy <https://w3id.org/probknow/resource/model/claude-fable-5-1> ;
    pk1:assessmentType "morphoeval/0.1.0/morphometric-validation" ;
    pk1:evidenceAgainst "2021-pringle-roman-esco-fractal-inflorescence.py L482–L518: Raw area-weighted box-count slope over 7 grids; Romanesco 1.95, Cauliflower 1.62 vs references 2.71 / 2.38 <https://github.com/fractastical/morpholib/blob/d58a084/2021-pringle-roman-esco-fractal-inflorescence.py#L482-L518>",
        "2021-pringle-roman-esco-fractal-inflorescence.py L818–L831: beta_emergent = slope_norm * v_r = 1.81 * 0.16 = 0.289 vs reference 0.085; implied v_r* reported <https://github.com/fractastical/morpholib/blob/d58a084/2021-pringle-roman-esco-fractal-inflorescence.py#L818-L831>",
        "2021-pringle-roman-esco-fractal-inflorescence.py L906–L923: lambda_emp from two fixed LoG scales (sigma 7 and 18 px) and NMS windows 17 / 39 px; value 0.390 tracks the sigma ratio 0.389 <https://github.com/fractastical/morpholib/blob/d58a084/2021-pringle-roman-esco-fractal-inflorescence.py#L906-L923>" ;
    pk1:hasEvidence <https://w3id.org/probknow/resource/evidence/morphoeval-pringle-roman-esco-fractal-inflorescence-measurement-ap1-cal-shoot-reversion-tfl1-steady>,
        <https://w3id.org/probknow/resource/evidence/morphoeval-pringle-roman-esco-fractal-inflorescence-measurement-ap1-cal-soc1-floral-memory-steady>,
        <https://w3id.org/probknow/resource/evidence/morphoeval-pringle-roman-esco-fractal-inflorescence-measurement-pin1-ablation-initiation-ratio>,
        <https://w3id.org/probknow/resource/evidence/morphoeval-pringle-roman-esco-fractal-inflorescence-measurement-pin1-coupled-tree-parastichy-sum>,
        <https://w3id.org/probknow/resource/evidence/morphoeval-pringle-roman-esco-fractal-inflorescence-measurement-pin1-emergent-divergence-angle-deg>,
        <https://w3id.org/probknow/resource/evidence/morphoeval-pringle-roman-esco-fractal-inflorescence-measurement-pin1-emergent-plastochron-acceleration-beta>,
        <https://w3id.org/probknow/resource/evidence/morphoeval-pringle-roman-esco-fractal-inflorescence-measurement-pin1-initiation-rate-vs-dome-radius-slope-normalised>,
        <https://w3id.org/probknow/resource/evidence/morphoeval-pringle-roman-esco-fractal-inflorescence-measurement-plastochron-sweep-aspect-ratio-pearson-r>,
        <https://w3id.org/probknow/resource/evidence/morphoeval-pringle-roman-esco-fractal-inflorescence-measurement-romanesco-3d-fractal-dimension-df>,
        <https://w3id.org/probknow/resource/evidence/morphoeval-pringle-roman-esco-fractal-inflorescence-measurement-romanesco-cone-aspect-ratio>,
