<https://w3id.org/delphi/resource/math-law/pringle-roman-esco-fractal-inflorescence-1> a skos:Concept,
        pk:Concept ;
    rdfs:label "Azpeitia et al. (2021) & Prusinkiewicz et al. (2007) AP1/CAL Floral GRN Bistability Collapse & Iterative Shoot Reversion Law" ;
    dct:description "Proves that loss of AP1/CAL in ap1 cal and Brassica curd mutants abolishes the floral commitment fixed point while preserving transient LFY-induced SOC1 floral memory (bract suppression) and high TFL1 shoot identity, causing recursive inflorescence branching | Variables: g_AP1 in {0, 1}: AP1/CAL locus functional dosage; L: LFY concentration; A: AP1/CAL floral commitment level; T: TFL1 shoot meristem identity factor; S: SOC1/AGL24/FUL floral memory factor" ;
    dct:source "Azpeitia et al. (2021) Science 373(6551):192-197 Figs. 1-2; Prusinkiewicz et al. (2007) Science 316:1452-1456" ;
    rdfs:seeAlso <https://github.com/fractastical/morpholib/blob/d58a084/2021-pringle-roman-esco-fractal-inflorescence.py#L163-L261>,
        <https://github.com/fractastical/morpholib/blob/d58a084/morphoeval/lean/loops/Loop_040_roman_esco_fractal_inflorescence.lean#L27-L56> ;
    skos:broader <https://w3id.org/delphi/resource/concept/math-of-biology> ;
    skos:definition """def ap1_steady (g_ap1 a_floral : Int) : Int := g_ap1 * a_floral
def tfl1_steady (t_shoot g_ap1 r_repress : Int) : Int := t_shoot - g_ap1 * r_repress
def soc1_memory (s_basal lfy_spike : Int) : Int := s_basal + lfy_spike
theorem azpeitia_2021_ap1_cal_grn_shoot_reversion
    (g_ap1 a_floral t_shoot r_repress s_basal lfy_spike : Int)
    (hg : g_ap1 > 0) (ha : a_floral > 0) (hr : r_repress > 0) (hlfy : lfy_spike > 0) :
    ap1_steady 0 a_floral = 0 ∧
    ap1_steady g_ap1 a_floral > 0 ∧
    tfl1_steady t_shoot 0 r_repress = t_shoot ∧
    tfl1_steady t_shoot 0 r_repress > tfl1_steady t_shoot g_ap1 r_repress ∧
    soc1_memory s_basal lfy_spike > s_basal
"""^^pk:lean4 ;
    skos:notation "d[AP1]/dt = g_AP1 (α_A L² + α_AA A²)/((1 + L² + A²)(1 + (T/K_TA)²)) - γ A;  g_AP1 = 0 ⇒ A* = 0, T* = T_shoot > T*_WT, S* = S_basal + ΔS_LFY > S_basal" ;
    prov:wasDerivedFrom <https://doi.org/10.1038/nature02081>,
        <https://doi.org/10.1073/pnas.0509839103>,
        <https://doi.org/10.1073/pnas.0510457103>,
        <https://doi.org/10.1103/PhysRevE.70.046109>,
        <https://doi.org/10.1103/PhysRevLett.68.2098>,
        <https://doi.org/10.1105/tpc.2.8.755>,
        <https://doi.org/10.1126/science.1140429>,
        <https://doi.org/10.1126/science.7824951>,
        <https://doi.org/10.1126/science.abg5935> ;
    schema:programmingLanguage "Lean 4" ;
    pk:hypothesisType "Coupled Floral Identity Gene-Regulatory Network (TFL1 -| LFY <-> AP1/CAL + SOC1/AGL24) & Recursive Spiral Phyllotaxis with Accelerating Plastochron" ;
    pk:leanDeclaration "MathOfBiology.Loop_040.ap1_steady" ;
    pk:leanTheorem "MathOfBiology.Loop_040.azpeitia_2021_ap1_cal_grn_shoot_reversion" ;
    pk:leanVerified true .

<https://w3id.org/delphi/resource/math-law/pringle-roman-esco-fractal-inflorescence-2> a skos:Concept,
        pk:Concept ;
    rdfs:label "Azpeitia et al. (2021) Accelerating Plastochron Quadratic Primordium Accumulation Law" ;
    dct:description "Proves that linear plastochron acceleration β > 0 generates a quadratic surplus of lateral meristems ½ β T² over constant-plastochron cauliflower (β = 0), shifting contact parastichy numbers from (8, 13) to (13, 21) | Variables: Δt(t): plastochron interval between consecutive lateral primordia; r_0 = 1/Δt_0: basal initiation rate; β: plastochron acceleration rate; N(T): cumulative primordia initiated by meristem age T" ;
    dct:source "Azpeitia et al. (2021) Science 373(6551):192-197 Figs. 3-4" ;
    rdfs:seeAlso <https://github.com/fractastical/morpholib/blob/d58a084/2021-pringle-roman-esco-fractal-inflorescence.py#L268-L336>,
        <https://github.com/fractastical/morpholib/blob/d58a084/morphoeval/lean/loops/Loop_040_roman_esco_fractal_inflorescence.lean#L72-L89> ;
    skos:broader <https://w3id.org/delphi/resource/concept/math-of-biology> ;
    skos:definition """def twice_primordia_count (r0 beta T : Int) : Int :=
  2 * r0 * T + beta * T * T
theorem azpeitia_2021_accelerating_plastochron_surplus (r0 beta T : Int)
    (hbeta : beta > 0) (hT : T > 0) :
    twice_primordia_count r0 0 T = 2 * r0 * T ∧
    twice_primordia_count r0 beta T - twice_primordia_count r0 0 T = beta * T * T ∧
    twice_primordia_count r0 beta T > twice_primordia_count r0 0 T
"""^^pk:lean4 ;
    skos:notation "Δt(t) = Δt_0 / (1 + β t),  r_p(t) = r_0 + β t  ⇒  N_Rom(T) = r_0 T + ½ β T² > r_0 T = N_Caul(T)  (for β > 0)" ;
    prov:wasDerivedFrom <https://doi.org/10.1038/nature02081>,
        <https://doi.org/10.1073/pnas.0509839103>,
        <https://doi.org/10.1073/pnas.0510457103>,
        <https://doi.org/10.1103/PhysRevE.70.046109>,
        <https://doi.org/10.1103/PhysRevLett.68.2098>,
        <https://doi.org/10.1105/tpc.2.8.755>,
        <https://doi.org/10.1126/science.1140429>,
        <https://doi.org/10.1126/science.7824951>,
        <https://doi.org/10.1126/science.abg5935> ;
    schema:programmingLanguage "Lean 4" ;
    pk:hypothesisType "Coupled Floral Identity Gene-Regulatory Network (TFL1 -| LFY <-> AP1/CAL + SOC1/AGL24) & Recursive Spiral Phyllotaxis with Accelerating Plastochron" ;
    pk:leanDeclaration "MathOfBiology.Loop_040.twice_primordia_count" ;
    pk:leanTheorem "MathOfBiology.Loop_040.azpeitia_2021_accelerating_plastochron_surplus" ;
    pk:leanVerified true .

<https://w3id.org/delphi/resource/math-law/pringle-roman-esco-fractal-inflorescence-3> a skos:Concept,
        pk:Concept ;
    rdfs:label "Azpeitia et al. (2021) Conical vs Hemispherical Curd Aspect Ratio Amplification Law" ;
    dct:description "Proves that conical height and height-to-radius aspect ratio H/R increase strictly monotonically with plastochron acceleration β, transforming a flat hemispherical cauliflower dome (β = 0, H/R ≈ 0.56) into a pointed self-similar Romanesco cone (β = 0.085, H/R ≈ 1.48) | Variables: H(β, T): axial height of meristematic cone; R: basal curd radius; dz: vertical internode displacement per plastochron acceleration unit; β: plastochron acceleration coefficient" ;
    dct:source "Azpeitia et al. (2021) Science 373(6551):192-197 Fig. 4" ;
    rdfs:seeAlso <https://github.com/fractastical/morpholib/blob/d58a084/2021-pringle-roman-esco-fractal-inflorescence.py#L340-L480>,
        <https://github.com/fractastical/morpholib/blob/d58a084/morphoeval/lean/loops/Loop_040_roman_esco_fractal_inflorescence.lean#L102-L131> ;
    skos:broader <https://w3id.org/delphi/resource/concept/math-of-biology> ;
    skos:definition """def curd_height (h0 dz beta T : Int) : Int :=
  h0 + dz * beta * T
theorem azpeitia_2021_conical_aspect_amplification (h0 dz beta1 beta2 T : Int)
    (hdz : dz > 0) (hT : T > 0) (hb1 : beta1 > 0) (hb12 : beta1 < beta2) :
    curd_height h0 dz 0 T = h0 ∧
    curd_height h0 dz beta1 T > h0 ∧
    curd_height h0 dz beta2 T - curd_height h0 dz beta1 T = dz * (beta2 - beta1) * T ∧
    curd_height h0 dz beta1 T < curd_height h0 dz beta2 T
"""^^pk:lean4 ;
    skos:notation "H(β, T) = H_0 + dz · β · T,  (H/R)(β_2) > (H/R)(β_1) > (H/R)(0) = H_0 / R_0  (for 0 < β_1 < β_2)" ;
    prov:wasDerivedFrom <https://doi.org/10.1038/nature02081>,
        <https://doi.org/10.1073/pnas.0509839103>,
        <https://doi.org/10.1073/pnas.0510457103>,
        <https://doi.org/10.1103/PhysRevE.70.046109>,
        <https://doi.org/10.1103/PhysRevLett.68.2098>,
        <https://doi.org/10.1105/tpc.2.8.755>,
        <https://doi.org/10.1126/science.1140429>,
        <https://doi.org/10.1126/science.7824951>,
        <https://doi.org/10.1126/science.abg5935> ;
    schema:programmingLanguage "Lean 4" ;
    pk:hypothesisType "Coupled Floral Identity Gene-Regulatory Network (TFL1 -| LFY <-> AP1/CAL + SOC1/AGL24) & Recursive Spiral Phyllotaxis with Accelerating Plastochron" ;
    pk:leanDeclaration "MathOfBiology.Loop_040.curd_height" ;
    pk:leanTheorem "MathOfBiology.Loop_040.azpeitia_2021_conical_aspect_amplification" ;
    pk:leanVerified true .

<https://w3id.org/delphi/resource/math-law/pringle-roman-esco-fractal-inflorescence-4> a skos:Concept,
        pk:Concept ;
    rdfs:label "Jönsson et al. (2006) Up-the-Gradient PIN1 Auxin Flux Law (Pass 3)" ;
    dct:description "Proves that linear up-the-gradient PIN1 allocation transports auxin toward the auxin-richer neighbour (destabilising feedback), which is what makes discrete auxin maxima and therefore primordia emerge on the epidermal mesh of the curd dome (`simulate_pin1_auxin_transport`); the T = 0 ablation (Reinhardt et al. 2003 pin1/NPA) removes the maxima | Variables: A_i: auxin concentration of epidermal cell i; P_ij: PIN1 efflux carrier on the wall of cell i facing neighbour j; P_tot: total PIN1 per cell; κ: allocation saturation; T: transport coefficient; D: apoplastic diffusion; c, d: auxin production and decay" ;
    dct:source "Jönsson et al. (2006) PNAS 103(5):1633-1638; Smith et al. (2006) PNAS 103(5):1301-1306; Reinhardt et al. (2003) Nature 426:255-260" ;
    rdfs:seeAlso <https://github.com/fractastical/morpholib/blob/d58a084/2021-pringle-roman-esco-fractal-inflorescence.py#L587-L777>,
        <https://github.com/fractastical/morpholib/blob/d58a084/morphoeval/lean/loops/Loop_040_roman_esco_fractal_inflorescence.lean#L141-L166> ;
    skos:broader <https://w3id.org/delphi/resource/concept/math-of-biology> ;
    skos:definition """def pin1_net_flux (a_i a_j : Int) : Int :=
  a_i * a_j * (a_j - a_i)
theorem jonsson_2006_up_gradient_pin1_flux (a_i a_j : Int)
    (hi : a_i > 0) (hj : a_j > 0) :
    pin1_net_flux a_i a_i = 0 ∧
    (a_i < a_j → pin1_net_flux a_i a_j > 0) ∧
    (a_j < a_i → pin1_net_flux a_i a_j < 0) ∧
    pin1_net_flux a_i a_j = - pin1_net_flux a_j a_i
"""^^pk:lean4 ;
    skos:notation "P_ij = P_tot A_j / (κ + Σ_k A_k),  J_{i→j} = T P_ij A_i  ⇒  two-cell net flux  J_net(a_i, a_j) = a_i a_j (a_j − a_i):  = 0 if a_i = a_j,  > 0 if a_j > a_i (up the gradient),  antisymmetric" ;
    prov:wasDerivedFrom <https://doi.org/10.1038/nature02081>,
        <https://doi.org/10.1073/pnas.0509839103>,
        <https://doi.org/10.1073/pnas.0510457103>,
        <https://doi.org/10.1103/PhysRevE.70.046109>,
        <https://doi.org/10.1103/PhysRevLett.68.2098>,
        <https://doi.org/10.1105/tpc.2.8.755>,
        <https://doi.org/10.1126/science.1140429>,
        <https://doi.org/10.1126/science.7824951>,
        <https://doi.org/10.1126/science.abg5935> ;
    schema:programmingLanguage "Lean 4" ;
    pk:hypothesisType "Coupled Floral Identity Gene-Regulatory Network (TFL1 -| LFY <-> AP1/CAL + SOC1/AGL24) & Recursive Spiral Phyllotaxis with Accelerating Plastochron" ;
    pk:leanDeclaration "MathOfBiology.Loop_040.pin1_net_flux" ;
    pk:leanTheorem "MathOfBiology.Loop_040.jonsson_2006_up_gradient_pin1_flux" ;
    pk:leanVerified true .

<https://w3id.org/delphi/resource/math-law/pringle-roman-esco-fractal-inflorescence-5> a skos:Concept,
        pk:Concept ;
    rdfs:label "Hofmeister / Douady-Couder Perimeter Scaling → Azpeitia (2021) Plastochron Acceleration (PIN1 mesh coupling, Pass 3)" ;
    dct:description "Couples the PIN1 epidermal mesh to the 3D meristem-tree plastochron law: the emergent slope k of r_p(R) measured on the mesh (`couple_pin1_mesh_to_plastochron`) and the meristem growth rate v_r determine β = (k / r_p(R_0)) v_r; the script reports β_emergent = 0.289 at the vendored v_r = 0.16 versus the reference 0.085 (implied v_r* = 0.047), an honest mismatch carried to Pass 4 | Variables: k: emergent initiation rate per unit dome radius measured on the PIN1 mesh (slope of r_p vs R); R_0: initial meristem radius; v_r: radial meristem expansion rate (vendored 0.16); t: meristem age; β: Law-2 plastochron acceleration" ;
    dct:source "Douady & Couder (1992) Phys. Rev. Lett. 68(13):2098-2101; Azpeitia et al. (2021) Science 373(6551):192-197 Figs. 3-4" ;
    rdfs:seeAlso <https://github.com/fractastical/morpholib/blob/d58a084/2021-pringle-roman-esco-fractal-inflorescence.py#L779-L862>,
        <https://github.com/fractastical/morpholib/blob/d58a084/morphoeval/lean/loops/Loop_040_roman_esco_fractal_inflorescence.lean#L181-L202> ;
    skos:broader <https://w3id.org/delphi/resource/concept/math-of-biology> ;
    skos:definition """def perimeter_rate (k R : Int) : Int :=
  k * R
def meristem_radius (R0 v t : Int) : Int :=
  R0 + v * t
theorem hofmeister_perimeter_plastochron_acceleration (k R0 v t : Int)
    (hk : k > 0) (ht : t > 0) :
    perimeter_rate k (meristem_radius R0 v t) = k * R0 + (k * v) * t ∧
    perimeter_rate k (meristem_radius R0 0 t) = k * R0 ∧
    (v > 0 → perimeter_rate k (meristem_radius R0 v t) > perimeter_rate k (meristem_radius R0 0 t)) ∧
    (v > 0 → k * v > 0)
"""^^pk:lean4 ;
    skos:notation "r_p(R) = k R  (initiation rate ∝ free perimeter of the initiation ring);  R(t) = R_0 + v_r t  ⇒  r_p(t) = k R_0 + (k v_r) t,  i.e. Law-2 r_0 = k R_0,  β = k v_r  (β > 0 ⇔ v_r > 0: Romanesco; β = 0 ⇔ v_r = 0: Cauliflower)" ;
    prov:wasDerivedFrom <https://doi.org/10.1038/nature02081>,
        <https://doi.org/10.1073/pnas.0509839103>,
        <https://doi.org/10.1073/pnas.0510457103>,
        <https://doi.org/10.1103/PhysRevE.70.046109>,
        <https://doi.org/10.1103/PhysRevLett.68.2098>,
        <https://doi.org/10.1105/tpc.2.8.755>,
        <https://doi.org/10.1126/science.1140429>,
        <https://doi.org/10.1126/science.7824951>,
        <https://doi.org/10.1126/science.abg5935> ;
    schema:programmingLanguage "Lean 4" ;
    pk:hypothesisType "Coupled Floral Identity Gene-Regulatory Network (TFL1 -| LFY <-> AP1/CAL + SOC1/AGL24) & Recursive Spiral Phyllotaxis with Accelerating Plastochron" ;
    pk:leanDeclaration "MathOfBiology.Loop_040.perimeter_rate" ;
    pk:leanTheorem "MathOfBiology.Loop_040.hofmeister_perimeter_plastochron_acceleration" ;
    pk:leanVerified true .

<https://w3id.org/probknow/resource/math-law/pringle-roman-esco-fractal-inflorescence-1> a skos:Concept,
        pk1:Concept ;
    rdfs:label "Azpeitia et al. (2021) & Prusinkiewicz et al. (2007) AP1/CAL Floral GRN Bistability Collapse & Iterative Shoot Reversion Law" ;
    dct:description "Proves that loss of AP1/CAL in ap1 cal and Brassica curd mutants abolishes the floral commitment fixed point while preserving transient LFY-induced SOC1 floral memory (bract suppression) and high TFL1 shoot identity, causing recursive inflorescence branching | Variables: g_AP1 in {0, 1}: AP1/CAL locus functional dosage; L: LFY concentration; A: AP1/CAL floral commitment level; T: TFL1 shoot meristem identity factor; S: SOC1/AGL24/FUL floral memory factor" ;
    dct:source "Azpeitia et al. (2021) Science 373(6551):192-197 Figs. 1-2; Prusinkiewicz et al. (2007) Science 316:1452-1456" ;
    rdfs:seeAlso <https://github.com/fractastical/morpholib/blob/d58a084/2021-pringle-roman-esco-fractal-inflorescence.py#L163-L261>,
        <https://github.com/fractastical/morpholib/blob/d58a084/morphoeval/lean/loops/Loop_040_roman_esco_fractal_inflorescence.lean#L27-L56> ;
    skos:broader <https://w3id.org/probknow/resource/concept/math-of-biology> ;
    skos:definition """def ap1_steady (g_ap1 a_floral : Int) : Int := g_ap1 * a_floral
def tfl1_steady (t_shoot g_ap1 r_repress : Int) : Int := t_shoot - g_ap1 * r_repress
def soc1_memory (s_basal lfy_spike : Int) : Int := s_basal + lfy_spike
theorem azpeitia_2021_ap1_cal_grn_shoot_reversion
    (g_ap1 a_floral t_shoot r_repress s_basal lfy_spike : Int)
    (hg : g_ap1 > 0) (ha : a_floral > 0) (hr : r_repress > 0) (hlfy : lfy_spike > 0) :
    ap1_steady 0 a_floral = 0 ∧
    ap1_steady g_ap1 a_floral > 0 ∧
    tfl1_steady t_shoot 0 r_repress = t_shoot ∧
    tfl1_steady t_shoot 0 r_repress > tfl1_steady t_shoot g_ap1 r_repress ∧
    soc1_memory s_basal lfy_spike > s_basal
"""^^pk1:lean4 ;
    skos:notation "d[AP1]/dt = g_AP1 (α_A L² + α_AA A²)/((1 + L² + A²)(1 + (T/K_TA)²)) - γ A;  g_AP1 = 0 ⇒ A* = 0, T* = T_shoot > T*_WT, S* = S_basal + ΔS_LFY > S_basal" ;
    prov:wasDerivedFrom <https://doi.org/10.1038/nature02081>,
        <https://doi.org/10.1073/pnas.0509839103>,
        <https://doi.org/10.1073/pnas.0510457103>,
        <https://doi.org/10.1103/PhysRevE.70.046109>,
        <https://doi.org/10.1103/PhysRevLett.68.2098>,
        <https://doi.org/10.1105/tpc.2.8.755>,
        <https://doi.org/10.1126/science.1140429>,
        <https://doi.org/10.1126/science.7824951>,
        <https://doi.org/10.1126/science.abg5935> ;
    schema:programmingLanguage "Lean 4" ;
    pk1:hypothesisType "Coupled Floral Identity Gene-Regulatory Network (TFL1 -| LFY <-> AP1/CAL + SOC1/AGL24) & Recursive Spiral Phyllotaxis with Accelerating Plastochron" ;
    pk1:leanDeclaration "MathOfBiology.Loop_040.ap1_steady" ;
    pk1:leanTheorem "MathOfBiology.Loop_040.azpeitia_2021_ap1_cal_grn_shoot_reversion" ;
    pk1:leanVerified true .

<https://w3id.org/probknow/resource/math-law/pringle-roman-esco-fractal-inflorescence-2> a skos:Concept,
        pk1:Concept ;
    rdfs:label "Azpeitia et al. (2021) Accelerating Plastochron Quadratic Primordium Accumulation Law" ;
    dct:description "Proves that linear plastochron acceleration β > 0 generates a quadratic surplus of lateral meristems ½ β T² over constant-plastochron cauliflower (β = 0), shifting contact parastichy numbers from (8, 13) to (13, 21) | Variables: Δt(t): plastochron interval between consecutive lateral primordia; r_0 = 1/Δt_0: basal initiation rate; β: plastochron acceleration rate; N(T): cumulative primordia initiated by meristem age T" ;
    dct:source "Azpeitia et al. (2021) Science 373(6551):192-197 Figs. 3-4" ;
    rdfs:seeAlso <https://github.com/fractastical/morpholib/blob/d58a084/2021-pringle-roman-esco-fractal-inflorescence.py#L268-L336>,
        <https://github.com/fractastical/morpholib/blob/d58a084/morphoeval/lean/loops/Loop_040_roman_esco_fractal_inflorescence.lean#L72-L89> ;
    skos:broader <https://w3id.org/probknow/resource/concept/math-of-biology> ;
    skos:definition """def twice_primordia_count (r0 beta T : Int) : Int :=
  2 * r0 * T + beta * T * T
theorem azpeitia_2021_accelerating_plastochron_surplus (r0 beta T : Int)
    (hbeta : beta > 0) (hT : T > 0) :
    twice_primordia_count r0 0 T = 2 * r0 * T ∧
    twice_primordia_count r0 beta T - twice_primordia_count r0 0 T = beta * T * T ∧
    twice_primordia_count r0 beta T > twice_primordia_count r0 0 T
"""^^pk1:lean4 ;
    skos:notation "Δt(t) = Δt_0 / (1 + β t),  r_p(t) = r_0 + β t  ⇒  N_Rom(T) = r_0 T + ½ β T² > r_0 T = N_Caul(T)  (for β > 0)" ;
    prov:wasDerivedFrom <https://doi.org/10.1038/nature02081>,
        <https://doi.org/10.1073/pnas.0509839103>,
        <https://doi.org/10.1073/pnas.0510457103>,
        <https://doi.org/10.1103/PhysRevE.70.046109>,
        <https://doi.org/10.1103/PhysRevLett.68.2098>,
        <https://doi.org/10.1105/tpc.2.8.755>,
        <https://doi.org/10.1126/science.1140429>,
        <https://doi.org/10.1126/science.7824951>,
        <https://doi.org/10.1126/science.abg5935> ;
    schema:programmingLanguage "Lean 4" ;
    pk1:hypothesisType "Coupled Floral Identity Gene-Regulatory Network (TFL1 -| LFY <-> AP1/CAL + SOC1/AGL24) & Recursive Spiral Phyllotaxis with Accelerating Plastochron" ;
    pk1:leanDeclaration "MathOfBiology.Loop_040.twice_primordia_count" ;
    pk1:leanTheorem "MathOfBiology.Loop_040.azpeitia_2021_accelerating_plastochron_surplus" ;
    pk1:leanVerified true .

<https://w3id.org/probknow/resource/math-law/pringle-roman-esco-fractal-inflorescence-3> a skos:Concept,
        pk1:Concept ;
    rdfs:label "Azpeitia et al. (2021) Conical vs Hemispherical Curd Aspect Ratio Amplification Law" ;
    dct:description "Proves that conical height and height-to-radius aspect ratio H/R increase strictly monotonically with plastochron acceleration β, transforming a flat hemispherical cauliflower dome (β = 0, H/R ≈ 0.56) into a pointed self-similar Romanesco cone (β = 0.085, H/R ≈ 1.48) | Variables: H(β, T): axial height of meristematic cone; R: basal curd radius; dz: vertical internode displacement per plastochron acceleration unit; β: plastochron acceleration coefficient" ;
    dct:source "Azpeitia et al. (2021) Science 373(6551):192-197 Fig. 4" ;
    rdfs:seeAlso <https://github.com/fractastical/morpholib/blob/d58a084/2021-pringle-roman-esco-fractal-inflorescence.py#L340-L480>,
        <https://github.com/fractastical/morpholib/blob/d58a084/morphoeval/lean/loops/Loop_040_roman_esco_fractal_inflorescence.lean#L102-L131> ;
    skos:broader <https://w3id.org/probknow/resource/concept/math-of-biology> ;
    skos:definition """def curd_height (h0 dz beta T : Int) : Int :=
  h0 + dz * beta * T
theorem azpeitia_2021_conical_aspect_amplification (h0 dz beta1 beta2 T : Int)
    (hdz : dz > 0) (hT : T > 0) (hb1 : beta1 > 0) (hb12 : beta1 < beta2) :
    curd_height h0 dz 0 T = h0 ∧
    curd_height h0 dz beta1 T > h0 ∧
    curd_height h0 dz beta2 T - curd_height h0 dz beta1 T = dz * (beta2 - beta1) * T ∧
    curd_height h0 dz beta1 T < curd_height h0 dz beta2 T
"""^^pk1:lean4 ;
    skos:notation "H(β, T) = H_0 + dz · β · T,  (H/R)(β_2) > (H/R)(β_1) > (H/R)(0) = H_0 / R_0  (for 0 < β_1 < β_2)" ;
    prov:wasDerivedFrom <https://doi.org/10.1038/nature02081>,
        <https://doi.org/10.1073/pnas.0509839103>,
        <https://doi.org/10.1073/pnas.0510457103>,
        <https://doi.org/10.1103/PhysRevE.70.046109>,
        <https://doi.org/10.1103/PhysRevLett.68.2098>,
        <https://doi.org/10.1105/tpc.2.8.755>,
        <https://doi.org/10.1126/science.1140429>,
        <https://doi.org/10.1126/science.7824951>,
        <https://doi.org/10.1126/science.abg5935> ;
    schema:programmingLanguage "Lean 4" ;
    pk1:hypothesisType "Coupled Floral Identity Gene-Regulatory Network (TFL1 -| LFY <-> AP1/CAL + SOC1/AGL24) & Recursive Spiral Phyllotaxis with Accelerating Plastochron" ;
    pk1:leanDeclaration "MathOfBiology.Loop_040.curd_height" ;
    pk1:leanTheorem "MathOfBiology.Loop_040.azpeitia_2021_conical_aspect_amplification" ;
    pk1:leanVerified true .

<https://w3id.org/probknow/resource/math-law/pringle-roman-esco-fractal-inflorescence-4> a skos:Concept,
        pk1:Concept ;
    rdfs:label "Jönsson et al. (2006) Up-the-Gradient PIN1 Auxin Flux Law (Pass 3)" ;
    dct:description "Proves that linear up-the-gradient PIN1 allocation transports auxin toward the auxin-richer neighbour (destabilising feedback), which is what makes discrete auxin maxima and therefore primordia emerge on the epidermal mesh of the curd dome (`simulate_pin1_auxin_transport`); the T = 0 ablation (Reinhardt et al. 2003 pin1/NPA) removes the maxima | Variables: A_i: auxin concentration of epidermal cell i; P_ij: PIN1 efflux carrier on the wall of cell i facing neighbour j; P_tot: total PIN1 per cell; κ: allocation saturation; T: transport coefficient; D: apoplastic diffusion; c, d: auxin production and decay" ;
    dct:source "Jönsson et al. (2006) PNAS 103(5):1633-1638; Smith et al. (2006) PNAS 103(5):1301-1306; Reinhardt et al. (2003) Nature 426:255-260" ;
    rdfs:seeAlso <https://github.com/fractastical/morpholib/blob/d58a084/2021-pringle-roman-esco-fractal-inflorescence.py#L587-L777>,
        <https://github.com/fractastical/morpholib/blob/d58a084/morphoeval/lean/loops/Loop_040_roman_esco_fractal_inflorescence.lean#L141-L166> ;
    skos:broader <https://w3id.org/probknow/resource/concept/math-of-biology> ;
    skos:definition """def pin1_net_flux (a_i a_j : Int) : Int :=
  a_i * a_j * (a_j - a_i)
theorem jonsson_2006_up_gradient_pin1_flux (a_i a_j : Int)
    (hi : a_i > 0) (hj : a_j > 0) :
    pin1_net_flux a_i a_i = 0 ∧
    (a_i < a_j → pin1_net_flux a_i a_j > 0) ∧
    (a_j < a_i → pin1_net_flux a_i a_j < 0) ∧
    pin1_net_flux a_i a_j = - pin1_net_flux a_j a_i
"""^^pk1:lean4 ;
    skos:notation "P_ij = P_tot A_j / (κ + Σ_k A_k),  J_{i→j} = T P_ij A_i  ⇒  two-cell net flux  J_net(a_i, a_j) = a_i a_j (a_j − a_i):  = 0 if a_i = a_j,  > 0 if a_j > a_i (up the gradient),  antisymmetric" ;
    prov:wasDerivedFrom <https://doi.org/10.1038/nature02081>,
        <https://doi.org/10.1073/pnas.0509839103>,
        <https://doi.org/10.1073/pnas.0510457103>,
        <https://doi.org/10.1103/PhysRevE.70.046109>,
        <https://doi.org/10.1103/PhysRevLett.68.2098>,
        <https://doi.org/10.1105/tpc.2.8.755>,
        <https://doi.org/10.1126/science.1140429>,
        <https://doi.org/10.1126/science.7824951>,
        <https://doi.org/10.1126/science.abg5935> ;
    schema:programmingLanguage "Lean 4" ;
    pk1:hypothesisType "Coupled Floral Identity Gene-Regulatory Network (TFL1 -| LFY <-> AP1/CAL + SOC1/AGL24) & Recursive Spiral Phyllotaxis with Accelerating Plastochron" ;
    pk1:leanDeclaration "MathOfBiology.Loop_040.pin1_net_flux" ;
    pk1:leanTheorem "MathOfBiology.Loop_040.jonsson_2006_up_gradient_pin1_flux" ;
    pk1:leanVerified true .

<https://w3id.org/probknow/resource/math-law/pringle-roman-esco-fractal-inflorescence-5> a skos:Concept,
        pk1:Concept ;
    rdfs:label "Hofmeister / Douady-Couder Perimeter Scaling → Azpeitia (2021) Plastochron Acceleration (PIN1 mesh coupling, Pass 3)" ;
    dct:description "Couples the PIN1 epidermal mesh to the 3D meristem-tree plastochron law: the emergent slope k of r_p(R) measured on the mesh (`couple_pin1_mesh_to_plastochron`) and the meristem growth rate v_r determine β = (k / r_p(R_0)) v_r; the script reports β_emergent = 0.289 at the vendored v_r = 0.16 versus the reference 0.085 (implied v_r* = 0.047), an honest mismatch carried to Pass 4 | Variables: k: emergent initiation rate per unit dome radius measured on the PIN1 mesh (slope of r_p vs R); R_0: initial meristem radius; v_r: radial meristem expansion rate (vendored 0.16); t: meristem age; β: Law-2 plastochron acceleration" ;
    dct:source "Douady & Couder (1992) Phys. Rev. Lett. 68(13):2098-2101; Azpeitia et al. (2021) Science 373(6551):192-197 Figs. 3-4" ;
    rdfs:seeAlso <https://github.com/fractastical/morpholib/blob/d58a084/2021-pringle-roman-esco-fractal-inflorescence.py#L779-L862>,
        <https://github.com/fractastical/morpholib/blob/d58a084/morphoeval/lean/loops/Loop_040_roman_esco_fractal_inflorescence.lean#L181-L202> ;
    skos:broader <https://w3id.org/probknow/resource/concept/math-of-biology> ;
    skos:definition """def perimeter_rate (k R : Int) : Int :=
  k * R
def meristem_radius (R0 v t : Int) : Int :=
  R0 + v * t
theorem hofmeister_perimeter_plastochron_acceleration (k R0 v t : Int)
    (hk : k > 0) (ht : t > 0) :
    perimeter_rate k (meristem_radius R0 v t) = k * R0 + (k * v) * t ∧
    perimeter_rate k (meristem_radius R0 0 t) = k * R0 ∧
    (v > 0 → perimeter_rate k (meristem_radius R0 v t) > perimeter_rate k (meristem_radius R0 0 t)) ∧
    (v > 0 → k * v > 0)
"""^^pk1:lean4 ;
    skos:notation "r_p(R) = k R  (initiation rate ∝ free perimeter of the initiation ring);  R(t) = R_0 + v_r t  ⇒  r_p(t) = k R_0 + (k v_r) t,  i.e. Law-2 r_0 = k R_0,  β = k v_r  (β > 0 ⇔ v_r > 0: Romanesco; β = 0 ⇔ v_r = 0: Cauliflower)" ;
    prov:wasDerivedFrom <https://doi.org/10.1038/nature02081>,
        <https://doi.org/10.1073/pnas.0509839103>,
        <https://doi.org/10.1073/pnas.0510457103>,
        <https://doi.org/10.1103/PhysRevE.70.046109>,
        <https://doi.org/10.1103/PhysRevLett.68.2098>,
        <https://doi.org/10.1105/tpc.2.8.755>,
        <https://doi.org/10.1126/science.1140429>,
        <https://doi.org/10.1126/science.7824951>,
        <https://doi.org/10.1126/science.abg5935> ;
    schema:programmingLanguage "Lean 4" ;
    pk1:hypothesisType "Coupled Floral Identity Gene-Regulatory Network (TFL1 -| LFY <-> AP1/CAL + SOC1/AGL24) & Recursive Spiral Phyllotaxis with Accelerating Plastochron" ;
    pk1:leanDeclaration "MathOfBiology.Loop_040.perimeter_rate" ;
    pk1:leanTheorem "MathOfBiology.Loop_040.hofmeister_perimeter_plastochron_acceleration" ;
    pk1:leanVerified true .

